nly non-obvious part.\n\n### Positive Findings\n\n- **`tui_model.go:73-78`** (`cancelling` field): textbook WHY comment — explains the double-Ctrl+C semantic that's invisible from the type.\n- **`tui_model.go:190-201`** (mouse routing): explicitly preempts the \"simplify into the catch-all\" temptation by spelling out the View.MouseMode dependency. Exactly the comment the task brief was worried about.\n- **`tui_model.go:411-419`** (`View` doc on MouseMode): rare case of explaining a library quirk (per-view vs Program option) that a maintainer would otherwise hit by trial-and-error.\n- **`tui_text.go:60-66`** (`wrapDisplayWidth`): documents the load-bearing newline-preservation behavior and the width&lt;=0 edge case. Meets the bar.\n- **`tui_sink.go:121-131`** + `139-141`: doc-comment commit is thorough; both the head comment and the inline `Wait()` comment are in sync.\n\n### Files Reviewed\n- /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/review-fix-2/.worktrees/review-fix-local/cmd/entire/cli/review/tui_sink.go\n- /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/review-fix-2/.worktrees/review-fix-local/cmd/entire/cli/review/tui_model.go\n- /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/review-fix-2/.worktrees/review-fix-local/cmd/entire/cli/review/tui_detail.go\n- /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/review-fix-2/.worktrees/review-fix-local/cmd/entire/cli/review/tui_text.go</result>\n<usage><total_tokens>58846</total_tokens><tool_uses>12</tool_uses><duration_ms>61671</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
