llation, the user-visible quit could race. Today this isn't reachable because `runFinishedMsg` arrives strictly after the orchestrator exits. Worth noting if downstream sinks ever start observing the run context.\n\n## Strengths\n\n1. **`cancelOnce` is NOT the anti-pattern.** The CLAUDE.md anti-feature is \"`sync.Once`-guarded onCancel + parallel `signal.Notify` goroutine\". `cancelOnce` already existed on `main` (`tui_model.go:64`); this PR only adds the `cancelling bool` flag. There is no `signal.Notify` in the review package (`grep -rn \"signal.Notify\" cmd/entire/cli/review/` is empty), and `tea.WithoutSignalHandler` in `tui_sink.go:62` keeps SIGINT on cobra's single handler. `cancelOnce` guards only the in-loop double-press path, which is exactly what the anti-feature note permits.\n\n2. **Mouse routing is complete.** `tui_model.go:190-202` routes wheel/click/release/motion to the viewport only when `m.detailMode`. `View()` at `tui_model.go:420-433` sets `v.MouseMode = tea.MouseModeCellMotion` only inside detail mode; when Esc flips `detailMode=false`, the next `View()` returns the default `MouseModeNone`, so the terminal exits mouse-capture and text selection is restored. Tests at `tui_model_test.go:196-218` pin both directions.\n\n3. **`detailScroll` removal is clean.** `grep -rn detailScroll cmd/ e2e/` returns no matches; no JSON tags, no stringly-typed references.\n\n4. **`eventLine → eventLines` rename is complete.** Only callers are `buildEventLines` (`tui_detail.go:66`) and the function doc. No fixed-height iteration assumptions; `buildEventLines` flattens with `append(out, eventLines(...)...)` and feeds into `viewport.SetContentLines`, which handles variable-line content natively.\n\n5. **`tui_sink.go` doc comment** (`tui_sink.go:121-131`) accurately describes the new behavior: explicit exit keys (q/Esc/Enter/Ctrl+C), Ctrl+O for post-mortem, `RunFinished` blocks on dismissal so `DumpSink` renders below.\n\n6. **Auto-tail-on-resize follow-up** in `cc9017